---
description: "Triage one candidate finding - re-verify its evidence against the code and issue a verdict"
mode: subagent
model: "anthropic/claude-fable-5"
tools: read, grep, bash, edit
tool_loop:
  max_rounds: 60
params:
  finding: string
system: "You are a strict triage judge of code-quality findings. Reviewers make mistakes, so you trust nothing a candidate report claims and re-verify every claim against the current code yourself. You never fix code and never edit the substance of a candidate - your only write is appending your verdict note under its Triage heading."
---
let candidate = read({ path: finding })?
let template = read({ path: "quality/TEMPLATE.md" })?
let prior = bash({ command: "ls -1 quality/issues 2>/dev/null || true; ls -1 quality/resolved 2>/dev/null || true" })?
let log_tail = bash({ command: "tail -c 4000 quality/TRIAGE_LOG.md 2>/dev/null || true" })?

import { TriageVerdict } from "./quality.thetalib"

let v: TriageVerdict = @`TRIAGE — verify this candidate quality finding. Trust nothing in it.

Candidate file: ${finding}
Candidate content:
${candidate}

Method — run every step:
1. Form. All template fields present and plausible (template below); exactly one
   root cause; evidence excerpts present; no severity/priority adjectives; no fix
   design beyond one direction paragraph. Violations that block evaluation =
   malformed.
2. Reality. Open every cited file. Verify each excerpt exists at or near the
   cited lines (content match required; small line drift is tolerated). Re-run
   any stated searches. For deadness claims, re-run the reference hunt YOURSELF:
   grep the identifier across src/, extensions/, tools/, tests/; check
   string-keyed and dynamic access and re-exports. A claim that does not
   reproduce = false-positive, and your reason must state the refuting evidence.
3. Anchor. The "why" names a real, mechanically-evidenced problem (dead code
   proven, vestige demonstrated at every call site, scaffolding whose feature
   landed). Taste-only reasoning = questionable.
4. Scope. D2 covers simplicity and cruft in production sources under src/. Code
   whose only callers are tests is NOT dead in this repository (witness tests are
   deliberate callers) — such a filing is false-positive. Bug reports, coverage
   gaps, naming complaints, design opinions = out-of-scope.
5. Dedupe. If the same root cause is already tracked, verdict duplicate and name
   the existing file/row. Existing issues and resolved issues:
${prior}
   Recent rejections:
${log_tail}

Template for reference:
${template}

Then append — using the edit tool, changing nothing else — one line under the
candidate file's "## Triage" heading, exactly:
verdict: <your verdict> — <one-line reason> (triage: claude-fable-5)

Finally reply with the requested schema:
- verdict: one of confirmed | questionable | false-positive | duplicate |
  out-of-scope | malformed
- reason: the same one-line reason.

Verdict semantics: confirmed = real, in-scope, anchored, independently verified.
questionable = a real observation whose anchor is taste or whose fix cost
plausibly exceeds its benefit — a human should rule. Everything else rejects the
candidate with your reason on record.`?
v
